      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we delegate identifying the nature of the fault all the way down to this function (which is confusing given the names of `handle_permission_fault` and `mark_dirty_block`), we do not want to return `Ok` if `!flags.contains(Attributes::DBM)` as that would ignore any actually permission violation (e.g. writing to read/execute-only memory) ... Do you have a way to identify if the fault was trigger by the DB without reading the PTE (e.g. from the ESR)?",
